    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Items or fluid",
      "text": [
        "Each second a relay moves up to **16 items** or **250 mB**.",
        "Item and Fluid relays carry what their name says. A **Water Seal** in the **Rune** slot makes any plate carry fluid; an **Earth Seal** makes it carry items.",
        "For fluid, park a Spirit Cistern at each end. Relays move fluid; they do not store it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Three distances",
      "text": [
        "- **Item** and **Fluid Relays** reach **32 blocks**. Base cost **4 Pulse** per beat that moves something.",
        "- **Longreach** relays reach **128 blocks**. Base cost **8**.",
        "- **Astral** relays have no distance limit and cross between worlds. Base cost **16**.",
        "The pack's consumption multiplier, **2.0** by default, doubles those. A beat that moves nothing costs nothing.",
        "Ranked plates (see [Machine ranks](machine_ranks)) pay **118%**, **143%** or **182%** of that and move as much more: about **19 / 23 / 29** items or **294 / 357 / 455 mB**. Pulse per item stays about even."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "The Lattice Tuner",
      "text": [
        "The other way to aim a plate. Right-click the face of the block you want goods delivered to; the tuner remembers that face. Then right-click the plate with the tuner to bind it. Mark the destination, never the plate.",
        "A tuner-bound plate needs an empty Bond slot, and the same distance limits apply.",
        "A tuner binding survives picking the plate up. Breaking a plate drops its Bond and Rune beside it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Controls and when it waits",
      "text": [
        "A steady redstone signal pauses a plate. Power the receiving plate, or the tuner's target block, to stop a transfer from the far end.",
        "A comparator on a plate reads **0** unlinked, **1** linked but waiting, **15** while moving cargo.",
        "Both ends must already be loaded. An unloaded or full destination makes the relay wait; nothing is ever voided. Relays never load chunks themselves, so put a Wayanchor at the far end if it must work while you are away.",
        "Crouch and right-click a plate with this book to see its link, cost and why it is waiting."
      ]
    },
